From 6a937e736f1bee4585baa2e8be869bc81639aa72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:45:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] VAX8200: Deliver DWBUA error and Unibus device interrupts
 at all BI levels

uba_eval_int() looped over IPL_HMAX - IPL_HMIN (3) levels and so never
raised IPL 17, the level VMS selects in the DWBUA's BIIC error interrupt
control register (EICR 000801D0).  An adapter (error) interrupt was then
left pending for ever, and because the Unibus device requests were only
passed on while no adapter interrupt was pending, no Unibus interrupt
reached the CPU any more.

VMS V4.7 triggers an adapter error during start-up (the UDA50, still
polling the rings set up by VMB, hits an invalid map register after VMS
reloads the map) and then hung after the banner: every UDA50
initialization timed out after its first step, as the step interrupt was
never delivered.

Now both the adapter interrupt (at the EICR levels) and the Unibus
device interrupts are evaluated over all IPL_HLVL levels, independently.
VMS V4.7 boots and runs on the VAX 8200 simulator; the diagnostic
supervisor test passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 VAX/vax820_uba.c | 35 ++++++++++++++++++++---------------
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/VAX/vax820_uba.c b/VAX/vax820_uba.c
index 9ee3516..fe67859 100644
--- a/VAX/vax820_uba.c
+++ b/VAX/vax820_uba.c
@@ -537,31 +537,36 @@ SET_IRQL;                                               /* update ints */
 return;
 }
 
-/* Update UBA nexus interrupts */
+/* Update UBA nexus interrupts
+
+   The adapter's own (error) interrupt is requested at the BI levels
+   selected in the error interrupt control register, the Unibus device
+   interrupts at their own levels; both are presented at the same time.
+
+   Earlier versions ran the level loops only
+   to IPL_HMAX - IPL_HMIN (3 levels) and missed IPL 17, which VMS selects
+   for the DWBUA error interrupt; the adapter interrupt was then never
+   delivered, and while it was pending no Unibus device interrupt was
+   passed on either (VMS V4.7 hung after the banner, its UDA50
+   initialization timing out every 15 seconds). */
 
 void uba_eval_int (void)
 {
 int32 i, lvl;
 
-// TODO: Check BIIC register?
-if (uba_int) {
+for (i = 0; i < IPL_HLVL; i++)                          /* clear all UBA req */
+    nexus_req[i] &= ~(1 << TR_UBA);
+if (uba_int) {                                          /* adapter int? */
     lvl = (uba_biic.eicr >> BIECR_V_LVL) & BIECR_M_LVL;
-    for (i = 0; i < (IPL_HMAX - IPL_HMIN); i++) {
-        if (lvl & (1u << i)) {
+    for (i = 0; i < IPL_HLVL; i++) {
+        if (lvl & (1u << i))
             nexus_req[i] |= (1 << TR_UBA);
-            }
         }
     }
-else {
-    for (i = 0; i < (IPL_HMAX - IPL_HMIN); i++)             /* clear all UBA req */
-        nexus_req[i] &= ~(1 << TR_UBA);
-    for (i = 0; i < (IPL_HMAX - IPL_HMIN); i++) {
-        if (int_req[i])
-            nexus_req[i] |= (1 << TR_UBA);
-        }
+for (i = 0; i < IPL_HLVL; i++) {                        /* Unibus device ints */
+    if (int_req[i])
+        nexus_req[i] |= (1 << TR_UBA);
     }
-//if (uba_int)                                            /* adapter int? */
-//    SET_NEXUS_INT (UBA);
 return;
 }
 
-- 
