From 644df090effed06a28ed5175305603686a778e4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:45:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] VAX8200: BICSR Start Self-Test also initializes the
 UNIBUS

BICSR bit 10 (BICSR_RST) is the BIIC's Start Self-Test bit.  On the DWBUA
it runs the self-test, which re-initializes the adapter, and the DWBUA
asserts UNIBUS AC LO, which initializes the UNIBUS as well
(EK-DWBUA-TM-001, sections 2.3.1 and 3.3.2 item 4).  The simulator only
reset the adapter, so Unibus devices kept their state: under VMS V4.7 the
UDA50 kept polling the rings set up by VMB, hit an invalid map register
after VMS had reloaded the map, and raised the DWBUA error interrupt that
exposed the interrupt level bug fixed in the previous commit.

Now the Unibus devices are reset too (uba_ubpdn), with UBPUP cleared
for the Unibus initialization time.  VMS V4.7 boots without the map
error.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 VAX/vax820_uba.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/VAX/vax820_uba.c b/VAX/vax820_uba.c
index fe67859..762c2b6 100644
--- a/VAX/vax820_uba.c
+++ b/VAX/vax820_uba.c
@@ -387,8 +387,17 @@ if (ofs >= UBAMAP_OF) {                                 /* map? */
 switch (ofs) {                                          /* case on offset */
 
     case BI_CSR:
-        if (val & BICSR_RST)                            /* unibus power init */
+        /* BICSR bit 10 (BICSR_RST here) is the BIIC's Start Self-Test
+           bit.  On the DWBUA it runs the self-test, which re-initializes
+           the adapter, and the DWBUA asserts UNIBUS AC LO, which also
+           initializes the UNIBUS (EK-DWBUA-TM-001, 2.3.1 and 3.3.2 item 4).
+           Earlier versions reset only the adapter, so Unibus devices
+           kept running with stale state (a UDA50 still polling the rings
+           set up by VMB hit an invalid map register under VMS). */
+        if (val & BICSR_RST) {                          /* start self-test */
             uba_reset (&uba_dev);                       /* reset adapter */
+            uba_ubpdn (uba_uitime);                     /* and init the UNIBUS */
+            }
         uba_biic.csr = (uba_biic.csr & ~BICSR_RW) | (val & BICSR_RW);
         break;
 
-- 
